	<h2>How are our programming courses different from a tutorial on the web?</h2>

	<h3>Step-by-step web programming</h3>

	<p>This is the first question you should ask yourself, and don't worry if you don't know the answer because confusing them is a very common mistake. The difference between our <strong>online courses</strong> and a tutorial on the web is called quality: the quality of showing unique content with skills in the IT sector, which will allow you to increase in a large percentage obtaining more job opportunities or your own ventures.</p>
	<div>
	<ul class="font-italic">
	    <li>Did you know that the word <strong>Open</strong>? Is widely used in the world of creating courses, for example English courses where we can mention <strong>Open English</strong>, therefore by following a course in <strong>OpenGisCRM</strong> you will be aiming for success in programming courses in English.</li>
		<br>
		<li>Were you aware that the word <strong>Gis</strong> ?, which means Geographic Information System is widely used in the world of web, desktop or mobile applications with extensions such as <strong>PostGIS</strong> with the use of relational databases <strong>PostgreSQL</strong> or <strong>MySQL</strong>, which when combined With libraries like <strong>Leaflet</strong> or <strong>OpenStreetMap</strong> you will enhance your geographic applications to the maximum.</li>
		<br>
		<li>Also, did you know that the word <strong>CRM</strong> ?, which means Customer relationship management is widely used in the world of creating programming codes, for example when creating CRM like <strong>Salesforce</strong>, so by acquiring some of our courses in English, you will have knowledge to start your own project in the cloud <strong>SAAS</strong> which stands for Software As A Service.</li>
		<br>							
	</ul>
	</div>	

